WEBVTT

00:13.660 --> 00:16.600
No, really! I only got 32 points.

00:16.600 --> 00:18.370
Then show me.

00:18.650 --> 00:21.530
You said we'd show each
other on the count of three.

00:21.530 --> 00:23.620
I showed you mine.

00:23.620 --> 00:26.630
I told you, I got 32 points...

00:26.960 --> 00:28.350
Then show me.

00:28.350 --> 00:30.210
I'm telling the truth!

00:30.210 --> 00:33.400
Think about it, it's 32 points.

00:33.400 --> 00:36.640
Why would I lie about such a realistic score?

00:36.640 --> 00:38.460
Just 32 points.

00:38.460 --> 00:40.230
Thirty-twelve!

00:40.230 --> 00:41.680
You mean thirty-two, right?

00:42.150 --> 00:45.510
So let's leave it at that, okay?

00:45.510 --> 00:46.940
Fine.

00:47.580 --> 00:50.930
It's not like seeing it will change anything.

00:50.930 --> 00:55.640
My score isn't that great either, so I got a little carried away...

00:55.640 --> 00:57.340
Gotcha!

01:03.580 --> 01:07.960
Everyday

01:04.580 --> 01:07.960
Compliments

01:15.340 --> 01:24.520
That's all I can do...

01:24.520 --> 01:28.650
Uh... this is, uh...

01:38.120 --> 01:40.130
Way to go, Yukko!

01:41.410 --> 01:42.900
No no no!

01:42.900 --> 01:45.100
I didn't mean "way to get a 1," I meant...

01:45.810 --> 01:49.410
Remember how you forgot your homework the day before yesterday?

01:53.850 --> 01:55.760
No, no. That's not what I meant!

01:55.760 --> 01:58.720
You did your homework but forgot to bring it in, right?

02:02.430 --> 02:03.940
So...?

02:04.220 --> 02:05.730
It's that mindset which counts!

02:06.390 --> 02:09.600
You don't usually do your homework, but that time you did!

02:10.160 --> 02:13.110
That's really hard to do.

02:13.110 --> 02:19.360
It's the same with dreams and ambitions. The first step is always the hardest.

02:19.660 --> 02:21.700
And you've done that, Yukko!

02:21.700 --> 02:24.830
You've cleared the hardest part!

02:25.570 --> 02:27.210
The hardest part?

02:27.360 --> 02:29.410
Yeah! The hardest part!

02:29.410 --> 02:30.920
The most difficult part!

02:31.230 --> 02:36.510
I... cleared... it?

02:36.760 --> 02:37.560
Yeah.

02:37.560 --> 02:41.430
You're amazing, Yukko, and you may not have noticed...

02:41.770 --> 02:45.430
But to a normal person, that's a really hard thing to accomplish!

02:46.250 --> 02:49.230
Well, I guess...

02:50.170 --> 02:51.300
...you're right!

02:52.130 --> 02:52.990
Yeah!

02:52.990 --> 02:54.090
Yeah, that's right!

02:54.090 --> 02:56.950
All jokes aside, I respect you for that.

02:56.950 --> 02:58.070
I guess.

02:58.070 --> 03:01.450
But you're definitely better than me, Mio-chan.

03:02.290 --> 03:05.080
After all, you always do your homework.

03:05.270 --> 03:08.280
It's just a habit to always do it.

03:08.280 --> 03:11.080
I'm doing homework as a habit.

03:11.080 --> 03:14.960
In your case, you're doing
something you don't usually do.

03:18.640 --> 03:20.120
This is...

03:22.940 --> 03:24.350
This bite...

03:25.280 --> 03:26.310
I've got her!

03:26.910 --> 03:29.210
But you know...

03:29.210 --> 03:30.690
Did you know this, Yukko?

03:30.960 --> 03:36.320
Trains and cars both use the most energy when they start moving.

03:36.600 --> 03:41.870
If you think about it that way, you may have immense amounts of power within you!

03:44.780 --> 03:46.200
I...

03:47.130 --> 03:48.290
...see!

03:50.520 --> 03:52.000
Don't fret.

03:52.000 --> 03:54.670
Little by little...

03:55.890 --> 03:59.420
But Mio-chan, you're giving me too much credit.

03:59.730 --> 04:02.270
I'm just a normal person.

04:02.270 --> 04:08.230
I fail a lot, and despite how I look, I get depressed a lot too.

04:08.230 --> 04:10.830
Oh, come on. There's no need to be so modest.

04:10.830 --> 04:12.560
I-I'm not being modest...

04:12.790 --> 04:16.440
Everyone already knows you're amazing.

04:18.270 --> 04:22.230
No, well... you know, the will to challenge yourself?

04:22.910 --> 04:25.700
I guess I can't say I don't have that at all...

04:26.010 --> 04:27.370
Right?

04:31.830 --> 04:34.210
I'm nothing compared to you.

04:34.210 --> 04:39.590
When I was working on my manga, I started to think, "this probably won't get an award."

04:39.590 --> 04:42.750
Then I got scared and never handed it in.

04:43.730 --> 04:46.050
Well, you <i>are a chicken.</i>

04:47.320 --> 04:50.720
Don't call me that, you 1-pointer...!

04:54.300 --> 04:56.270
Yukko, come here.

04:59.190 --> 04:59.900
Read this!

05:00.430 --> 05:02.280
Test ethics.

05:02.280 --> 05:05.400
Number one: Always try your best.

05:05.400 --> 05:07.390
Yes! That's exactly it!

05:07.390 --> 05:09.700
That's the most important thing!

05:09.700 --> 05:12.200
Yukko, you're always trying your best!

05:12.200 --> 05:14.870
You're already doing the most important thing!

05:15.050 --> 05:16.370
But I only got 1 point...

05:19.060 --> 05:21.590
I-I can't...

05:24.270 --> 05:25.720
I'm sorry, Yukko!

05:25.960 --> 05:30.560
I got carried away with grades and forgot about what's important.

05:30.560 --> 05:34.310
I guess I was a little jealous of you, since you're already golden!

05:34.310 --> 05:35.980
Er, but...

05:36.300 --> 05:38.750
Since I'm always doing my homework as a habit,

05:38.750 --> 05:41.890
I don't know really know if I'm giving the tests my all.

05:41.890 --> 05:42.940
The same goes for my manga.

05:43.200 --> 05:44.860
But Yukko, you're different.

05:44.860 --> 05:46.860
You're always trying your best!

05:49.280 --> 05:50.700
You're like a fresh breath of mountain air!

05:55.960 --> 06:01.000
I really want some of your positive attitude.

06:01.000 --> 06:04.310
But that's all I have.

06:04.310 --> 06:06.970
I told you, that's what's important!

06:08.710 --> 06:12.470
Well, I suppose you're right.

06:15.150 --> 06:18.730
How did you gain the confidence to take that first step?

06:18.960 --> 06:20.710
Simple.

06:20.710 --> 06:24.090
Though I shouldn't really brag about it.

06:24.090 --> 06:27.970
I guess you just have to avoid thinking negatively.

06:27.970 --> 06:30.070
You need to do your best to look straight ahead.

06:30.680 --> 06:34.140
It's important to know what you
believe in and that you won't lose.

06:34.140 --> 06:35.300
Something like that.

06:35.300 --> 06:36.870
Straight ahead?

06:37.050 --> 06:41.250
Well, in my case, I guess that came out subconsciously.

06:41.490 --> 06:43.420
Perhaps that's my natural disposition.

06:43.420 --> 06:46.850
Or maybe even...

06:47.220 --> 06:48.130
A talent.

06:49.500 --> 06:51.680
That's your talent, Yukko!

06:51.910 --> 06:54.560
No, no. It's not a talent.

06:55.630 --> 06:58.060
But maybe...

06:58.520 --> 07:02.480
I guess that's what it... is.

07:02.710 --> 07:06.600
If it's part of your subconscious, then it's something you were born with.

07:06.600 --> 07:09.530
It's not something you can acquire just by trying!

07:09.530 --> 07:11.860
I'm jealous of your innate talent!

07:11.990 --> 07:14.240
Innate Talent

07:14.910 --> 07:16.990
Genius

07:20.000 --> 07:21.420
Oh, Mio-chan!

07:21.570 --> 07:23.330
Are you <i>really Mio-chan?</i>

07:24.310 --> 07:26.790
Maybe I'll give you 100 yen! Just kidding!

07:27.690 --> 07:29.280
What are you doing?

07:29.970 --> 07:33.050
I'm trying to receive as much of your good fortune as possible.

07:33.890 --> 07:35.900
No way, no way, no way!

07:35.900 --> 07:37.970
There's no way I could give good fortune!

07:38.740 --> 07:40.300
That's not true.

07:40.300 --> 07:43.190
You're probably spreading
happiness around as we speak.

07:43.450 --> 07:44.770
Really?

07:44.770 --> 07:49.800
But they do say to give everything a try.

07:49.800 --> 07:52.030
I don't really get it, but...

07:52.300 --> 07:54.670
Maybe I got some.

07:54.670 --> 07:56.120
The courage to take the first step, that is!

07:56.280 --> 07:59.250
Gosh, you're not going to get anywhere by complimenting me so much!

07:59.250 --> 08:01.000
Did some of my motivation rub off on you?

08:01.000 --> 08:04.290
I told you, that motivation is what's best!

08:11.790 --> 08:12.810
All right!

08:12.810 --> 08:16.930
I can't sulk around over getting 1 point.

08:23.990 --> 08:25.540
I got away with it!

08:26.240 --> 08:29.370
I knew her depression was nothing to worry about.

08:30.110 --> 08:33.280
She'll bite right away if you set it up just right.

08:33.280 --> 08:36.220
Well, all I did was compliment the heck out of her.

08:36.220 --> 08:40.170
I just hope it leads to her studying a bit more.

08:41.620 --> 08:42.660
Mio-chan.

08:42.930 --> 08:45.670
I turned the source of this whole ordeal into a paper airplane.

08:47.160 --> 08:49.310
By sending this flying...

08:49.310 --> 08:52.300
I, too, will fly towards greater heights.

08:55.600 --> 08:57.190
This is denial.

08:58.130 --> 09:00.140
Here I go.

09:00.510 --> 09:02.520
Good-bye, oh light of youth!

09:08.660 --> 09:09.640
Owie.

09:23.810 --> 09:27.750
Nano, what are we going to play?

09:27.790 --> 09:31.380
An Everyday
Cold

09:38.480 --> 09:40.580
Here, blow your nose.

09:43.290 --> 09:45.430
Let's give you some medicine, Professor.

09:45.690 --> 09:47.270
What are we going to play?

09:47.820 --> 09:49.740
Please, drink your medicine.

09:49.740 --> 09:51.570
Sakamoto, what are we going to play?

09:52.570 --> 09:53.570
Let me think...

09:53.570 --> 09:54.900
Sakamoto-san!

09:54.900 --> 09:55.860
Why me?!

09:56.670 --> 10:00.620
You've had a runny nose since yesterday.

10:01.210 --> 10:04.620
I told you to go to bed, but you wouldn't listen.

10:04.620 --> 10:07.380
You won't even eat meals regularly.

10:08.580 --> 10:09.250
Here it is.

10:10.010 --> 10:12.690
I'm going to go play over there.

10:12.690 --> 10:14.130
No.

10:14.640 --> 10:18.440
I'll go get the water, so make sure to take it.

10:19.970 --> 10:25.430
But he said I wasn't really sick, so I don't have to take any medicine.

10:25.430 --> 10:26.270
Who did?

10:26.460 --> 10:27.530
Sakamoto.

10:27.530 --> 10:28.230
I never said that!

10:28.470 --> 10:29.870
Sakamoto-san!

10:29.870 --> 10:31.230
I said I didn't!

10:31.440 --> 10:36.850
Sakamoto said he loves medicine, so he wants to drink mine too.

10:36.850 --> 10:38.110
When was this?

10:38.110 --> 10:39.750
Sakamoto-san!

10:39.750 --> 10:41.120
You're seriously believing her?!

10:41.710 --> 10:46.490
And Sakamoto likes medicine so even if you say no-

10:53.040 --> 10:54.610
Blow.

10:56.540 --> 10:59.030
Anyway, drink your medicine.

10:59.030 --> 11:01.930
You won't get any better if you don't.

11:01.930 --> 11:06.850
But the medicine's kind of bitter.

11:06.850 --> 11:08.240
You'll be fine.

11:08.240 --> 11:11.620
It will all be gone in no time, okay?

11:12.720 --> 11:13.940
You're lying.

11:13.940 --> 11:15.320
I'm not lying.

11:15.320 --> 11:17.040
Yes you are!

11:17.040 --> 11:20.050
Last time, it didn't go away in no time.

11:20.050 --> 11:24.530
All right, if you have this you'll be better in no time.

11:25.060 --> 11:26.120
Does it taste good?

11:26.120 --> 11:30.840
I wrapped it in a wafer so that you won't taste it.

11:30.840 --> 11:33.500
All you have to do is swallow it.

11:33.820 --> 11:34.750
That's suspicious...

11:35.360 --> 11:37.910
Here. Say, "Ah."

11:40.410 --> 11:42.680
All right, just swallow it.

11:50.430 --> 11:53.480
No, you have to swallow it down with water!

11:54.570 --> 11:57.510
Quick, or the wafer's going to melt and-

12:03.980 --> 12:05.870
Nano, you liar.

12:06.180 --> 12:08.660
That was because you wouldn't swallow it right away.

12:09.270 --> 12:11.300
Geez, what a brat.

12:11.300 --> 12:12.980
Leave this one to me.

12:13.390 --> 12:14.780
Are you sure?

12:14.780 --> 12:15.670
Just watch.

12:15.960 --> 12:17.470
Hey, brat.

12:18.890 --> 12:21.010
You like sharks, don't you?

12:21.010 --> 12:22.510
Sharks?

12:22.510 --> 12:23.860
Yeah.

12:23.860 --> 12:27.650
Did you know that sharks hardly ever get sick?

12:27.650 --> 12:28.550
Really?

12:28.550 --> 12:29.470
Yeah.

12:29.470 --> 12:32.520
Even if they get scratched, their injuries go away like magic.

12:32.700 --> 12:35.020
People are different, however.

12:35.020 --> 12:37.980
That's because we aren't as cool as sharks.

12:37.980 --> 12:39.320
Yeah.

12:39.320 --> 12:42.480
So humans have to eat a lot of different things.

12:42.480 --> 12:45.400
When they get sick, they have to take-

12:45.400 --> 12:46.430
Take!

12:53.020 --> 12:54.750
Sakamoto-san!

12:56.270 --> 12:59.230
Professor, I'll take some with you.

12:59.230 --> 13:01.210
So please, have your medicine.

13:03.280 --> 13:04.680
We'll do it together!

13:05.200 --> 13:11.100
Since I can't bear it and Nano can, Nano should drink all of it!

13:11.100 --> 13:13.260
That's not how it works.

13:13.260 --> 13:15.480
Then Sakamoto should take it.

13:16.110 --> 13:17.900
What's the point of having me take it?!

13:18.550 --> 13:22.400
Your cold won't get better if you keep this up!

13:22.690 --> 13:26.250
I don't care if my cold doesn't get better...

13:28.720 --> 13:32.100
Sakamoto-san, grab me a tissue please.

13:32.100 --> 13:33.160
Sure thing.

13:37.670 --> 13:39.260
Sakamoto-san!

13:39.260 --> 13:41.090
Crap! I can't stop!

13:44.220 --> 13:48.200
No, you'll dirty your coat if you wipe it there!

13:48.200 --> 13:50.210
It's not dirty!

13:50.210 --> 13:52.430
And I'm not going to take the medicine!

13:53.720 --> 13:55.110
Fine.

13:55.110 --> 13:58.060
If you won't take your medicine, then we won't have any snacks today.

13:59.130 --> 14:02.320
What a waste, I even made pudding.

14:02.810 --> 14:04.780
Pudding...

14:05.050 --> 14:07.700
He said I could eat a snack!

14:07.700 --> 14:09.900
Who did?!

14:11.180 --> 14:13.160
Are you going to blame me again?!

14:15.830 --> 14:16.960
Geez.

14:21.830 --> 14:23.920
She won't even eat her meals?

14:24.380 --> 14:25.420
No.

14:26.730 --> 14:28.560
Geez.

14:28.560 --> 14:30.470
Come here, girl.

14:32.600 --> 14:34.550
This is your fault, you know.

14:34.550 --> 14:38.940
Even if you force her, that brat won't take her medicine.

14:39.210 --> 14:41.000
I know.

14:41.000 --> 14:43.190
But I don't know what to do.

14:43.660 --> 14:46.660
Convincing her is going to be difficult.

14:47.030 --> 14:48.280
There's only one way.

14:48.280 --> 14:49.530
There is?

14:52.370 --> 14:53.780
Mix it in her snack.

14:55.390 --> 14:56.900
I see!

14:56.900 --> 15:01.540
Dock it on her favorite food and
camouflage it like a ride-on thing.

15:01.540 --> 15:03.430
We'll call it Operation Snack Mash-Up.

15:03.430 --> 15:06.770
Great idea, Sakamoto-san! You're a master strategist!

15:07.230 --> 15:09.050
You're hopeless without me.

15:09.050 --> 15:11.640
I'll go make it right away.

15:12.260 --> 15:13.320
Wait!

15:13.320 --> 15:14.100
Yes?

15:14.360 --> 15:16.380
You only have one chance.

15:16.380 --> 15:18.030
You won't get a second one if she catches on.

15:18.030 --> 15:19.180
Understood?

15:19.850 --> 15:20.910
Yes!

15:21.600 --> 15:25.390
Shark... Shark...

15:25.390 --> 15:26.690
Professor!

15:26.940 --> 15:27.940
Here she comes.

15:28.140 --> 15:30.700
It's snack time.

15:30.850 --> 15:32.670
Would you like some pudding?

15:34.560 --> 15:35.580
Really?!

15:35.880 --> 15:37.000
Yes.

15:37.000 --> 15:38.620
Eat up.

15:38.850 --> 15:39.830
Pudding!

15:42.500 --> 15:45.090
It's in plain sight!

15:45.580 --> 15:47.380
Come here, girl!

15:48.460 --> 15:50.260
Oh man, that scared me.

15:51.690 --> 15:53.290
Are you nuts?!

15:53.290 --> 15:55.510
Do you <i>want her to see it?!</i>

15:55.510 --> 15:57.010
Did I mess up?

15:57.220 --> 15:59.510
I told you that you only had one chance!

15:59.510 --> 16:01.770
Anyone would doubt that to be whipped cream!

16:02.360 --> 16:04.770
You have to mix it, mix it, and sprinkle it inside!

16:04.970 --> 16:07.730
Sorry, I'll mix it right away.

16:09.570 --> 16:14.620
Geez, you guys are useless without me.

16:15.290 --> 16:18.410
Good thing I'm around-

16:16.760 --> 16:18.030
Sakamoto-san!

16:29.230 --> 16:30.400
Delicious!

16:30.400 --> 16:31.240
Seriously?!

16:31.240 --> 16:33.130
This pudding is great.

16:33.130 --> 16:36.120
It's kind of crunchy, but then it becomes all pudding-like.

16:36.120 --> 16:38.140
R-Really?

16:38.140 --> 16:39.710
Thank goodness!

16:39.710 --> 16:41.690
Eat it all up.

16:43.400 --> 16:45.470
We did it, Sakamoto-san.

16:46.820 --> 16:51.240
Well, I guess this happens once in a while too.

16:56.520 --> 16:59.050
Nano, can I have one more?

16:59.050 --> 17:00.850
Crunchy pudding!

17:00.850 --> 17:01.690
Sure thing.

17:01.690 --> 17:04.270
But the next one isn't going to be crunchy.

17:04.270 --> 17:08.690
Why?! Sakamoto said he wanted crunchy pudding.

17:08.690 --> 17:09.520
Why me again?

17:08.840 --> 17:13.720
Shinonome Laboratory had yet another peaceful day.

17:09.520 --> 17:10.970
Sakamoto-san!

17:23.140 --> 17:26.730
Everyday
Reserving

17:31.830 --> 17:32.780
Huh?

17:32.780 --> 17:35.530
The train should be coming soon, right?

17:35.530 --> 17:38.020
Yeah, in about a minute.

17:47.710 --> 17:49.210
There's nobody here!

17:49.210 --> 17:50.580
Seems like it.

17:50.580 --> 17:53.090
There aren't many people around in the afternoon.

17:53.400 --> 17:55.540
Do we have the whole place to ourselves?

17:56.450 --> 17:57.540
In that case...

18:00.130 --> 18:02.760
Nobody will get angry if I do this?

18:02.760 --> 18:05.100
Wow, Yukko.

18:05.300 --> 18:08.130
You too, Mio-chan.

18:08.130 --> 18:10.200
Nobody seems to be around, anyway.

18:10.200 --> 18:11.980
R-Really?

18:11.980 --> 18:12.820
Okay.

18:13.030 --> 18:14.670
Here I go!

18:16.930 --> 18:18.420
How was that?!

18:18.420 --> 18:20.340
Mio-chan, that's wrong!

18:23.290 --> 18:24.410
It's here.

18:35.730 --> 18:38.330
Mai-chan, do you like trains?

18:38.880 --> 18:40.200
Somewhat.

18:48.880 --> 18:51.520
Nobody's here! It's like we reserved it!

18:55.480 --> 18:57.830
I'm really getting fired up now!

18:59.840 --> 19:03.900
Mio-chan, let's do the pushing game!

19:06.240 --> 19:07.510
Here we go.

19:07.510 --> 19:09.120
One, two...

19:17.130 --> 19:19.580
Mai-chan, you're the judge!

19:19.580 --> 19:20.630
Make sure you watch...

19:31.040 --> 19:32.270
Bunk bed.

19:37.080 --> 19:38.530
Triple bunk bed!

19:48.470 --> 19:54.230
For some reason, I feel like I'm the only one who's losing out.

19:58.710 --> 20:04.680
An Everyday
Episode 0

